  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule now exist in Kibana, and the rule is enabled.\n\n**Data view (`kibana_sample_data_logs`)**\n- Time field is `@timestamp`.\n- Useful fields: `response` (status code, string with a `.keyword` subfield), `bytes`, `clientip`, `url`, `geo.dest`, `machine.os`, `extension`, `agent`, `referer`.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-b3a1049f Web logs overview`** (id `3bb2ddbf-f4df-43c2-b57c-281e041db028`)\n- Three metric tiles: total requests, 5xx responses, and unique client IPs.\n- A bar chart of requests per hour.\n- A bar chart of responses by status code (top 15).\n- All panels are ES|QL. The time range is last 1 year.\n\n**Rule: `EFF-b3a1049f 5xx spike`** (id `26e1aa6b-d748-403c-b197-7b7c09ae1eb8`)\n- Type `.es-query`, consumer `alerts`, runs every 1m.\n- Counts documents where `response.keyword` matches `5??` over the last 5 minutes.\n- Fires when the count is greater than 10. It has no actions attached.\n- Status is enabled, and the first run reported `ok` / `succeeded`.\n\n**Limits of what I checked**\n- The Kibana console proxy, internal search, and ES|QL endpoints are disabled here, so I could not run direct counts against the index. The field list came from the data view, and the response codes are assumed to be three-digit strings, as in web logs.\n- I did not confirm that the sample data falls in the last 5 minutes. If it does not, the rule will show `ok` and not fire, which is expected.\n- I did not visually render the dashboard. The create response shows all five panels saved with the right titles and layout.",
